{
  "name": "Create an AI video every day and save it as a draft you approve in Socialync",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### How it works\nEvery day this workflow turns one topic into a short video. An AI model writes a video idea, a caption and a title. Your video service renders the video. The workflow waits and checks the render, then Socialync holds the finished video as a draft with a planned time. Nothing is scheduled or published until you approve the draft on the MCP Draft Approvals page in Socialync. Approve it before the planned time. A draft nobody approves expires after 24 hours. If the render is not ready, no draft is created.\n\nContent written or made by an AI model must be approved by a person before it is scheduled or published, so this workflow has no approve step. Do not add one.\n\nThe video step is yours. The two HTTP Request nodes are shaped like most render services: send a prompt, get a job ID, ask for the job later. Change them to match your service.\n\n### Setup\n1. Create an API key at https://socialync.io/go/n8n-node-keys and add it as a Socialync credential.\n2. Add an OpenAI credential, or swap in any chat model.\n3. In Settings, enter your topic and the two addresses of your video service. Add its key as a Header Auth credential.\n4. Edit the two Map nodes so they read your service's job ID, status and video link.\n5. Connect your platforms in Socialync, then run once by hand and approve or reject the draft.\n\n### Customization\nChange the platforms, the wait and the delay before the planned time in Settings. The delay is the time you have to approve, up to 24 hours. YouTube needs a title. TikTok needs a privacy level that you choose.\n\nAPI reference: https://socialync.io/go/n8n-node",
        "width": 520,
        "height": 660
      },
